; ============================================================
; TITLE:    A House on a Hill
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     rectangle, triangle, filled, picture
; SUMMARY:  Builds a colored house with a roof, door, windows, chimney and a sun out of simple shapes.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A whole picture made from rectangles and one triangle: a red
;   roof, yellow walls, a door, two windows, a chimney, green grass
;   and a round sun.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the numbers in the main part at the bottom
;   to move things around or paint them other colors.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a RECTANGLE procedure with two inputs: width and height
;   * FILLED color [ ... ] paints the inside of the shape the turtle walks
;   * thinking of a picture as a list of simple shapes
;   * a big DOT with a thick pen makes a round sun
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Paint the door blue: change [120 60 20] in the DOOR line.
;   * Add a third window.
;   * Make the house wider by changing 220 in WALLS and in ROOF.
; ============================================================

; Width first, then height. The turtle starts at the bottom left
; corner facing up and comes back to the same place.
to rectangle :width :height
  repeat 2 [forward :height right 90 forward :width right 90]
end

; A filled rectangle with a dark outline round it.
to box :x :y :width :height :color
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 0 pendown
  setpencolor [60 40 30]
  filled :color [rectangle :width :height]
end

; The roof is a triangle that sits on the top of the walls.
; We walk to the peak and back down with SETXY.
to roof :x :y :width :peak
  penup setxy :x :y pendown
  setpencolor [60 40 30]
  filled [190 40 40] [
    setxy :x + :width / 2 :y + :peak
    setxy :x + :width :y
    setxy :x :y
  ]
end

to sun :x :y
  penup setxy :x :y
  setpencolor [255 200 0]
  setpensize 70
  dot pos
  setpensize 3
end

; Shapes are painted in order, and each new one covers whatever is
; already there, like a painter working on a canvas. So the big wall
; goes first and the door and windows go on top of it. The chimney
; goes before the roof so the roof hides its bottom end.
to house
  box 55 40 30 60 [140 70 50]              ; chimney
  box -110 -150 220 150 [250 220 120]      ; walls
  roof -130 0 260 110
  box -30 -150 50 90 [120 60 20]           ; door
  box -90 -70 45 45 [150 210 255]          ; left window
  box 45 -70 45 45 [150 210 255]           ; right window
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3
sun 260 200
; the grass is one wide rectangle, painted before the house so the
; house stands on top of it
box -400 -300 800 150 [110 190 80]
house
hideturtle
